1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,216
Slide 8 explains "THE PARADIGM SHIFT: 'ASK ME' VS.

2
00:00:06,216 --> 00:00:07,260
'RUN IT'."

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:16,929
Examine the left card tagged "OLD PARADIGM": "Reactive Chatbot ('Ask Me')." In this traditional model, the system is completely passive.

4
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:28,730
The human must initiate every prompt, wait for tokens to stream across the screen, copy the response, manually paste it into another tool, and repeat the loop hundreds of times a day.

5
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:40,592
Look at the right card tagged "NEW PARADIGM": "Proactive Avatar ('Run It')." In our modern agentic architecture, the human provides a high-level goal or registers a scheduled event trigger.

6
00:00:40,592 --> 00:00:52,310
The agent takes sovereign operational control, queries live APIs, persists state to a database, handles network timeouts automatically, and only notifies the human when executive decisions are required!

7
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:59,792
Think about the cognitive difference: in the old world, you are a worker tethered to a keyboard.

8
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:05,140
In the new world, you are an executive architect directing autonomous systems.

9
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:12,593
In practical engineering terms, an 'Ask Me' chatbot requires an active HTTP socket and human presence.

10
00:01:12,593 --> 00:01:17,990
A 'Run It' avatar is a decoupled cloud micro-service with self-healing capabilities.

11
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:26,230
This is the core shift that empowers a single engineer to accomplish what previously required an entire operations team.

